        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "5c8faa6f-cc90-52ee-8d73-f34b4f47ee29",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harold Godwinson, Harald Hardrada, William the Conqueror, Tostig Godwinson, Eystein Orre\n- Events: Battle of Stamford Bridge, Battle of Hastings\n- Places: Stamford Bridge, East Riding of Yorkshire, England, Norway\n\nFacts:\n- On 25 September 1066, the Battle of Stamford Bridge took place at the village of Stamford Bridge in the East Riding of Yorkshire, England.\n- On 25 September 1066, an English army under King Harold Godwinson fought an invading Norwegian force led by King Harald Hardrada and Tostig Godwinson at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.\n- On 25 September 1066, Harold Godwinson defeated and killed Harald Hardrada at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.\n- On 25 September 1066, the Norwegian noble Eystein Orre was killed at the Battle of Stamford Bridge.\n- In the following month, William the Conqueror defeated and killed Harold Godwinson at the Battle of Hastings.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
